# A season word that is also a common verb. Wiktionary, s.v. "fall", verb
# sense 1 "(heading, intransitive) To be moved downwards." with the
# sub-sense "To come down, to drop or descend."; noun sense "(chiefly North
# America, archaic in Britain) The time of the year when the leaves typically
# fall from the trees; autumn; ..." (https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fall).
# Such a word reads as the season after a preposition, an article or "this",
# "next" or "last" (see marker_season_lead.voc), before a year, the solar
# event or a noun or predicate word of marker_season_follow.voc, with a part
# of the period ("late fall"), beside another season, or alone.
fall
